# Line endings are a repository invariant here, not a local preference.
#
# Several gates compare committed artifacts as *bytes*, so the bytes a checkout produces are part
# of the contract:
#
#   * `component_licenses_manifest_matches_committed_file` (crates/audio/candle-audio-catalog)
#     asserts `release/model-weight-licenses.json` equals what the catalog emits, and the emitter
#     writes LF.
#   * `scripts/release/build_release.py` digests the working-copy `Cargo.lock` into a release
#     manifest's `lockfile.sha256`, while the source archive beside it comes from `git archive`
#     (index bytes). A CRLF working copy makes those two disagree about the same file.
#
# With no attributes file and `core.autocrlf=true` — the Git for Windows install default — every
# text path checks out CRLF while the index holds LF, so those gates read bytes that never existed
# in the repository. The licence gate then fails on any Windows checkout with "…is stale", which is
# indistinguishable from real drift: the failure a contributor sees is identical whether or not the
# manifest actually needs regenerating. Linux CI stays green, so nothing catches it.
#
# `eol=lf` overrides `core.autocrlf`, so this holds for every contributor without anyone editing
# their Git config. It changes no committed bytes: the index was already LF for all 2897 text
# paths — only the checkout was wrong.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary payloads: never convert, never diff.
#
# `text=auto` guesses from the first 8000 bytes, and a .safetensors file opens with a long ASCII
# JSON header — a small enough tensor payload can leave that window free of NUL, so the guess can
# come back "text" and the eol rewrite would corrupt the weights. These are explicit for that
# reason; do not rely on detection for a format whose header is text.
*.safetensors binary
*.bytes       binary
*.gguf        binary
*.npy         binary
*.npz         binary
*.pt          binary
*.pth         binary
*.bin         binary

# Media and archives.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.wav  binary
*.flac binary
*.mp3  binary
*.mp4  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
*.tar  binary
